infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Where property tests pay — and where examples win
  desc Same suite, two surfaces: spend a property only where an invariant is simpler than the code
  compares
    - label Properties pay — math core
      children
        - label Parsers and serializers
          desc roundtrip: parse(dump(x)) == x
        - label Money and unit arithmetic
          desc oracle against a slow Decimal reference
        - label Normalizers and sanitizers
          desc idempotence: f(f(x)) == f(x)
        - label Codecs, date and timezone math
          desc a crisp invariant plus an inverse
    - label Examples win — CRUD surface
      children
        - label Thin CRUD glue
          desc the only property restates the mock
        - label Handler returns the row
          desc generation adds runtime, not falsification power
        - label No invariant simpler than the code
          desc a property re-deriving the impl verifies nothing
        - label Example tests are cheaper
          desc and honest enough for the CRUD surface
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f59e0b
